error Failure { Failed; }

// `source.branch.v1` after card `IF-ARMS`: an early `return` from a branch arm.
//
// The arm that returns discharges its custody at its *own* exit — `drop a;`
// before `return 1;` — which is exactly what the sequential route requires at
// any exit. It therefore never reaches the join, and the join is taken over the
// arms that survive to it. Here there is one survivor, so the statements after
// the branch belong to it: the driver lowers them inside the `else` arm, which
// is where they run, and every checked model then sees a branch both of whose
// arms end the function.
//
// Removing either `drop a;` is the conditional leak through an early return,
// and it refuses — at that exit rather than at the join.
fn main() -> i32 {
    let a = qcore_acquire(1, true, Failure);
    if (3 < 5) {
        drop a;
        return 1;
    }
    drop a;
    return 0;
}
